---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Downloads">
	<div class="container downloads-container">
		<h1 class="serif">Downloads</h1>
		<p class="lede">Central hub for all downloadable framework assets.</p>

		<div class="download-grid">
			<div class="card card-warm">
				<div class="eyebrow mono">v0.1</div>
				<h3 class="serif">Blank Starter Kit</h3>
				<p>The minimal directory structure and empty project brain templates to start a new ADDF project.</p>
				<a href="/Autonomous-Duck-Development-Framework/assets/starter-kit-blank-v0.1.zip" class="btn btn-primary" style="margin-top: var(--space-4);">Download ZIP →</a>
			</div>

			<div class="card">
				<div class="eyebrow mono">v0.1</div>
				<h3 class="serif">Example-Filled Starter Kit</h3>
				<p>The structure pre-populated with the Mini Task Tracker example to demonstrate the framework at scale.</p>
				<a href="/Autonomous-Duck-Development-Framework/assets/starter-kit-example-v0.1.zip" class="btn btn-secondary" style="margin-top: var(--space-4);">Download ZIP</a>
			</div>

			<div class="card">
				<div class="eyebrow mono">v0.1</div>
				<h3 class="serif">Prompt Catalog</h3>
				<p>The complete collection of copy-ready prompts grouped by mode: Research, Design, Develop, and Handoff.</p>
				<a href="/Autonomous-Duck-Development-Framework/assets/prompt-catalog-v0.1.zip" class="btn btn-secondary" style="margin-top: var(--space-4);">Download ZIP</a>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</Layout>

<style>
	.downloads-container {
		padding: var(--space-10) var(--space-5);
	}

	.lede {
		font-size: 20px;
		color: var(--ink-soft);
		margin-bottom: var(--space-8);
	}

	.download-grid {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
		gap: var(--space-6);
	}

	.download-grid .card h3 {
		font-size: 32px;
		margin-top: var(--space-2);
		margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
	}

	.download-grid .card p {
		color: var(--ink-soft);
	}

	@media (max-width: 959px) {
		.download-grid {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr;
		}
	}
</style>
